# Lazy Stoner Donator Agent Scope

- Use `.agents/` as project-specific operating briefs for strategy, copy, product proof, and release QA.
- Keep `.agents/` aligned with the current repo architecture. This project is a static HTML/CSS/JS wishlist frontend, not Shopify, SvelteKit, or a backend-heavy app.
- Repo files and `.cursor/rules/` remain the source of truth for implementation details; `.agents/` should guide decision flow, priorities, and checks.
- Do not reintroduce foreign assumptions, unrelated brands, mismatched stacks, or copied KPIs into this directory.
- When a repeated lesson becomes stable and implementation-facing, encode it in `.cursor/rules/` instead of overloading the agent brief.
- If an agent brief conflicts with the repo or current rules, update the agent brief before using it again.
